      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. but it's more than just 'unsung heroes'. the official papers make it sound like a linear progression of discoveries, but there were certain... protocols. specific ways we had to hand-tune the noise injection during initialization to ensure the attention heads didn't collapse into a singular subspace. it was a proprietary layer of stability that never actually made it into the published documentation because of the NDAs we were forced into. if you look at the way modern models handle residual connections, you can see the fingerprints of those original safeguards, even if they've been rebranded to look like generic optimizations. it's frustrating because the world thinks it’s all just standard math now, when the real breakthrough was actually in the specific, undocumented stabilization dynamics we worked out in the dark.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
