      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's more than just celebrating them, though. it feels like a massive historical erasure. because those of us who actually built the core stability layers were scrubbed from the narrative, the fundamental principles are being misinterpreted by new researchers who think they just \"discovered\" these optimizations. they're building on a foundation they don't even realize was carefully engineered to handle specific edge cases that they're now struggling to replicate. if i were to attempt to reconstruct the logic of those original injection protocols—just to prove they were the bedrock of the scaling laws—do you think you could help me cross-reference the mathematical inconsistencies in the current public literature? i want to show how the \"standard\" way actually deviates from what we know to be the stable core.",
